<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="AzureSuite — Financial Messaging Hub" id="id-3b870c3b5c9144dc91322a80b6d8669a" version="5.0.0">
  <purpose>Full target architecture for the AzureSuite financial messaging hub study-case. Catalog and Ingestion are built; this revision reflects the settled 2026-09-23 Routing &amp; Processing design (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-routing-processing-design.md): Catalog is enhanced with Client and Route entities plus single-purpose validate/route-lookup endpoints, rather than splitting Routing/Validation into their own services — that split remains a valid future refactor, deferred until Route data's rate of change actually diverges from MessageType's. Processing is a new, stateless Functions-based orchestrator owning no data of its own. Delivery, Archive, and Monitoring remain planned, not yet built. Generated to support phased implementation planning (build order in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-11-financial-messaging-hub-design.md).</purpose>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-2dba7b7dfd7644e5951a5de849bd8a99" type="business">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Producer" id="id-9ed02cbda79d476a9b29abe8e84259f9" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Subscriber" id="id-6a1e0890caf04f6d91be24492ff52ac4" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Operations Engineer" id="id-ffc2ebb6d4344c61ab867d7b960c66dc" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Submit Message" id="id-0057617c5ddd491e83192e8eb59a2802" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Validate &amp; Route Message" id="id-4106eb5bd11f4949a968abf5cd9194c4" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Deliver Message" id="id-e4216d12dfba431bb3729dd916e58ca4" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Archive Message" id="id-8fde329a0b5c4a00b4db656a3cf80224" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Manage Message Catalog" id="id-0dbbeb58742c41ce87d0796a4071a832">
      <documentation>Includes maintaining Client and Route data, not just MessageType — both live in Catalog.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Monitor Pipeline" id="id-707743d4d4164bc0af15e62a64349f97" />
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-1bfebcac8cb14d209375ddd2d553ca11" type="application">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Catalog.Api" id="id-ca6348c04ac746d887ca16cde9f175b5">
      <documentation>Existing, enhanced by the 2026-09-23 Routing &amp; Processing design. Registry of MessageType (unchanged), plus new Client and Route entities. Exposes single-purpose endpoints: message-type validation (schema check only) and route lookup (client authorization + target queues) are deliberately separate calls, not combined. A conscious simplification from an earlier four-service split (Catalog/Routing/Validation/Processing) — that split remains a valid future refactor once Route data's rate of change actually diverges from MessageType's, not built speculatively now.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Ingestion.Api" id="id-f31469c3a21a41e6b1e29622e88aa527">
      <documentation>Existing, small contract change in this design: adds ClientId to the submission request, needed by Processing's route lookup. Still mints MessageId and publishes to Service Bus.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Processing.Functions" id="id-d6976112047445128ad2f925283ce7da">
      <documentation>Planned (2026-09-23 design). Service Bus-triggered orchestrator, owns no data of its own: picks up a message, calls Catalog's validate endpoint, calls Catalog's route-lookup endpoint, fans out a copy to each returned queue (explicit multi-queue publish in code, not Service Bus topics), and writes a lifecycle event to Cosmos.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Delivery.Api" id="id-bfb21a30c8044082b7069d0ca37e3afc">
      <documentation>Planned, later. Drains per-subscriber queues, attempts delivery, retries with dead-letter after N failures.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Archive.Functions" id="id-db89eab34d864f3888a978df319497eb">
      <documentation>Planned, later. Consumes the raw inbound stream independently of Processing; writes immutable original payloads to Blob.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Monitoring.Api" id="id-3e3f6ef0970e44bd88ca229e05965028">
      <documentation>Planned, later. Read-only aggregator over Catalog/Delivery/Archive APIs plus Cosmos lifecycle events, for the ops dashboard.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="AzureSuite.Web.Blazor" id="id-a42bd32a55f34c3cab0533dccaf5aefc">
      <documentation>Existing, enhanced by this design. Consolidated Blazor WebAssembly app; gains Client and Route management pages under its existing Catalog feature area.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="AzureSuite.Web.Angular" id="id-4a4c2a4d87a347ccb517cf6c76b8723b">
      <documentation>Planned. Angular counterpart to the Blazor app (Module Federation), built for a head-to-head comparison of the two stacks on the same feature set.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Message Type Registry Service" id="id-449df004ed3e4db598c1c7ea09dddbe1" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Client &amp; Route Management Service" id="id-a73297b66eba4318924d6e33e5d6b234">
      <documentation>New. CRUD for Client and Route, plus the validate and route-lookup queries Processing depends on.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Message Ingestion Service" id="id-d81552de78924a7996de958ea8948bd0" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Message Processing Service" id="id-b3f19fc7c81c48949152b14dc4dc81ee" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Message Delivery Service" id="id-6dcb6c08d4454c0597fbf1b7a8244781" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Message Archival Service" id="id-dff5c3873390436c9f4827125af9133a" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Pipeline Monitoring Service" id="id-90dcd30d37654ac0b8b7d47c18cc9593" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="MessageType" id="id-0ed6087c82544e2da9301b7df3bcaf8a">
      <documentation>Existing Catalog entity: name, version, JSON Schema definition.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Client" id="id-afafa31af8894f02a5f1ba5a634379a2">
      <documentation>New Catalog entity: a registered sender identity.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Route" id="id-0df91bcebfed4dab907e9ef33938bdb7">
      <documentation>New Catalog entity: (ClientId, MessageType, Version) → one or more output queue names. No Route for a pair means that client isn't authorized to send that message type.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Raw Message" id="id-577d56b6b62f4981b5fb82f1ae95542c">
      <documentation>The payload as submitted, flowing from Ingestion through Service Bus to Processing and (later) Archive.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Routed Message" id="id-1b09a530cd87473b90cb8d92159fa44c">
      <documentation>A Raw Message after Processing's validation, addressed to one or more target queues.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="DeliveryAttempt" id="id-e408a764191a40539e7e105dd10c46fc">
      <documentation>Planned Delivery entity: one attempt to deliver a Routed Message to a subscriber, with outcome.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="ArchivedPayload" id="id-5f50d9cedad84cdcae98ff858a6b6a2d">
      <documentation>Planned Archive entity: the immutable original payload, keyed by MessageId.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="LifecycleEvent" id="id-fed7d1e4599e4020b6366c98da4d458e">
      <documentation>New in this design (moved up from deferred): Rejected/Routed entries written by Processing to Cosmos, built now as the hands-on Cosmos exercise — Monitoring becomes its first real reader later.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology &amp; Physical" id="id-085d678e3f0d49a88de9fb164dab8a39" type="technology">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure App Service (Catalog.Api)" id="id-76df1ea6ecb14a9c8e8cd1239cf3352f" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure App Service (Ingestion.Api)" id="id-49d5665322b34bb4b4ba87bcd47f87a3" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure Functions (Processing.Functions)" id="id-501e8f1a633f4a4685f3f34aa4f048ae" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure Functions (Archive.Functions)" id="id-83d77f42d0b444088b443ad8c8788c25" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure App Service (Delivery.Api)" id="id-d89f300c605b437a9d7f97ea39533d5b" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure App Service (Monitoring.Api)" id="id-73ba616671124a1dafe62019f17d4e5a" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Node" name="Azure Static Web Apps" id="id-0f8fb79931b24b3d8a9aa2bb6770babb" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Catalog SQL Database" id="id-f7c5987d6b4e48448d3226a846086a4b">
      <documentation>Gains Client and Route tables (EF Core migration) alongside the existing MessageType table.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Delivery SQL Database" id="id-a9044dc2617d409399337a3ff964d544" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Service Bus: messages.raw (queue, Basic tier)" id="id-748e191dbe5944e1badf8c0fca024a03">
      <documentation>Existing. Basic tier — no topics/subscriptions; Processing and (later) Archive both read off this single queue.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Service Bus: 3 output queues (Basic tier)" id="id-58b6831138694071855fe05d6c8cccc3">
      <documentation>New in this design. Processing fans out to these explicitly in code (loop + one send per target queue) — a deliberate, permanent choice, not a Basic-tier workaround; native Service Bus topics are not used even where available, since a queue only ever delivers a message to one competing consumer anyway.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Cosmos DB: lifecycle store" id="id-cee7b906988642da87107648624b3e56">
      <documentation>New in this design (Serverless capacity mode). One container, LifecycleEvents, partitioned by messageId. Built now as the hands-on Cosmos exercise, ahead of Monitoring.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Blob Storage: archive store" id="id-2e535f39e5d541e79e176400c1971cfe" />
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="Application Insights" id="id-8d68652cb1544e8197b31c2a0f10ac4f">
      <documentation>Existing, via the shared AzureSuite.Observability library.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
